OL,3,AMicrosoft 'deeply sorry' for global
OL,4,Aoutage as it reports broad recovery
OL,5,
OL,6,FMicrosoft has said it is "deeply sorry"
OL,7,Ffor the service outage to its products,
OL,8,Fincluding Outlook and Teams, which has
OL,9,Fcaused disruption around the world.
OL,11,FServices were broadly recovering by
OL,12,FFriday afternoon, nearly 24 hours after
OL,13,Fissues began. Microsoft said it was
OL,14,Fmaking "encouraging progress", but
OL,15,Fadded it does not know when services
OL,16,Fwill fully recover.
OL,23,APub: 13-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,110,105,200,160,0,100
