OL,3,AMicrosoft 'deeply sorry' for global
OL,4,Aoutage as it reports broad recovery
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe outage hit more than 70 countries,
OL,7,Fdisrupting everything from business
OL,8,Foperations to government services and
OL,9,Fpersonal users. More than 430 million
OL,10,Fpeople use the affected products
OL,11,Fworldwide.
OL,13,FMicrosoft said it was a technical issue
OL,14,Fintroduced during a "network capacity
OL,15,Fupgrade" and not related to cyber or
OL,16,Fartificial intelligence agents.
